{"uid":"b495c8d495b84294","name":"test_a_repoint_that_repairs_nothing_is_refused_and_never_repeatable","fullName":"tests.test_worker_split_proposal#test_a_repoint_that_repairs_nothing_is_refused_and_never_repeatable","historyId":"d16ce859469511adc847374a6b341d03","time":{"start":1791968933501,"stop":1791968933502,"duration":1},"description":"Every re-point must DROP a dead edge, and one that does also clears\n    the standing a second would need -- the two halves of the stagnation\n    bound, in one node because they are one property: a `dependsOn` edit\n    reads as progress (it edits an EXISTING row, so unlike an inserted split\n    task it is NOT filtered out of the pass's progress diff by\n    `state.tasks_doc_excluding_new_entries`, pinned above), so an entry that\n    can be re-sent is a free `stagnant` reset on tap.\n\n    Half one, the drop-at-least-one guard (#209 defect 7, unit 6 review):\n    `TRANS` below is doomed only THROUGH a live sibling, so its own list\n    holds no dead edge -- the live-drop and dead-edge guards are both\n    vacuous for it, and before this guard a replacement byte-identical to\n    its current list was ACCEPTED, writing the row, emitting a\n    `task.dependency_repointed` recording a re-point of nothing (`removed`\n    and `added` both empty), and -- since the target stays in\n    `task_blocked_by`'s map -- re-sendable for as many free resets as the\n    budget allows. An adds-only entry was accepted the same way. Both are\n    refused, naming the only thing that does clear such a task: re-pointing\n    the live dependency that is itself the doomed one.\n\n    Half two: after a re-point that DOES clear the doom, the same task is no\n    longer a key of the derived map, so asking again is refused for want of\n    standing, and putting the dead edge back is refused twice over. Between\n    the two halves an accepted re-point is never repeatable on one task at\n    all -- it leaves no dead edge for a second entry to drop -- which is why\n    `worker_repoint_budget_per_approach` (pinned in the budget node below,\n    and end to end in the stagnation node) bounds re-points across DIFFERENT\n    tasks rather than backstopping a treadmill on one.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Every re-point must DROP a dead edge, and one that does also clears<br />\nthe standing a second would need -- the two halves of the stagnation<br />\nbound, in one node because they are one property: a <code>dependsOn</code> edit<br />\nreads as progress (it edits an EXISTING row, so unlike an inserted split<br />\ntask it is NOT filtered out of the pass's progress diff by<br />\n<code>state.tasks_doc_excluding_new_entries</code>, pinned above), so an entry that<br />\ncan be re-sent is a free <code>stagnant</code> reset on tap.</p>\n<pre><code>Half one, the drop-at-least-one guard (#209 defect 7, unit 6 review):\n`TRANS` below is doomed only THROUGH a live sibling, so its own list\nholds no dead edge -- the live-drop and dead-edge guards are both\nvacuous for it, and before this guard a replacement byte-identical to\nits current list was ACCEPTED, writing the row, emitting a\n`task.dependency_repointed` recording a re-point of nothing (`removed`\nand `added` both empty), and -- since the target stays in\n`task_blocked_by`'s map -- re-sendable for as many free resets as the\nbudget allows. An adds-only entry was accepted the same way. Both are\nrefused, naming the only thing that does clear such a task: re-pointing\nthe live dependency that is itself the doomed one.\n\nHalf two: after a re-point that DOES clear the doom, the same task is no\nlonger a key of the derived map, so asking again is refused for want of\nstanding, and putting the dead edge back is refused twice over. Between\nthe two halves an accepted re-point is never repeatable on one task at\nall -- it leaves no dead edge for a second entry to drop -- which is why\n`worker_repoint_budget_per_approach` (pinned in the budget node below,\nand end to end in the stagnation node) bounds re-points across DIFFERENT\ntasks rather than backstopping a treadmill on one.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791968776884,"stop":1791968776885,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791968776885,"stop":1791968776885,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791968933492,"stop":1791968933492,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791968933492,"stop":1791968933495,"duration":3},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791968933495,"stop":1791968933495,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791968933496,"stop":1791968933499,"duration":3},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_undo_instant_sleep_patches","time":{"start":1791968933499,"stop":1791968933499,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps"